description:
Implement `useCallbackRef` — a hook that returns a callback ref (a function, not an object) which fires the provided callback with the element when it mounts, and with `null` when it unmounts.

**Example:**
```tsx
const ref = useCallbackRef((el) => {
  if (el) el.focus();
});
return <input ref={ref} />;
```

